{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_deathwatch", "label": "Death watch (context.watch)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Supervision is for a child failing, which is the parent problem; death watch is for an actor stopping, which is a notification any other actor can subscribe to. Registration sends nothing to the watched actor."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_terminated", "label": "Terminated message", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Arrives through the mailbox, so ordering with user messages is well-defined. existenceConfirmed is currently always true and addressTerminated always false \u2014 do not branch on either as a signal."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_watchwith", "label": "context.watchWith", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Moves the decision to registration time so the watcher receives a message of its own protocol; Terminated never enters the union, and the message is recorded in the watcher so nothing new goes on the wire."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_death_watch_unwatch", "label": "context.unwatch", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/death-watch.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Idempotent, and unnecessary before stopping \u2014 registrations are cleaned up automatically. It is for an actor that changes 